{
  "_comment": [
    "R-126 (CL-BUG-164): an `add_output` whose stateValues list is SHORTER than",
    "the contract's mutable-property list. `a` and `b` are both mutable; this",
    "node names only `t13` (the new `a`).",
    "",
    "The source pipeline counts addOutput arity in the typechecker (N20, N23,",
    "N26). --ir runs no frontend, so the node reaches stack lowering, where every",
    "tier serialized with a `i < len(stateValues) && i < len(stateProps)` loop --",
    "the min() of the two, silently. Measured before the fix, same file through",
    "every --ir CLI:",
    "  go / rust / zig / ruby   compiled clean, 1388 hexchars where the correct",
    "                           two-value node produces 1394: an output whose",
    "                           OP_RETURN payload carries ONE state field when",
    "                           deserialize_state will slice TWO at fixed offsets",
    "  python                   TypeError out of its own lowering",
    "  java                     produced no script",
    "",
    "A continuation committing to a short state payload is spendable only by a",
    "hand-crafted transaction -- every SDK's StateSerializer writes ALL mutable",
    "fields -- and the successor it produces is permanently unspendable, because",
    "the next call's deserialize_state slices at fixed offsets. Every tier must",
    "refuse it."
  ],
